; Test whether an object is shut in by a closed holder
;
; Follows the chain of holders (record +1) upward from the object in A through
; holders whose flag bit 5 (active, open, alive) is set. Reaching an object
; that lies at a location (holder AT_LOCATION) means it is in the open. A
; holder with bit 5 clear stops the chain. #R$8EEC calls it for the subject
; (an actor) and returns when the answer is NZ.
; .
; A Object id
; O:F Z set when the chain ends at a location, NZ when a holder with bit 5 clear is met
; O:A AT_LOCATION when Z; the id of that holder OR 1 when NZ
; Preserves IX.
@label=CheckEnclosed
c$8ED2 PUSH IX        ;
 $8ED4 CALL $9BCA     ; IX := record of A
@label=CheckEnclosed_Next
*$8ED7 LD A,(IX+$01)  ; holder id
@isub=CP AT_LOCATION
 $8EDA CP $FF         ;
 $8EDC JR Z,$8EE9     ;
 $8EDE CALL $9BCA     ; IX := record of the holder
@isub=BIT FLAG_ACTIVE,(IX+$07)
 $8EE1 BIT 5,(IX+$07) ;
 $8EE5 JR NZ,$8ED7    ;
 $8EE7 OR $01         ; make A non-zero: NZ
*$8EE9 POP IX         ;
 $8EEB RET            ;
